					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/k-class-complete-list</guid>
				<title>A Comprehensive List of K-Class Scenarios</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/k-class-complete-list</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;image-container floatright&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/k-class-complete-list/k-class2.png&quot; width=&quot;305px&quot; alt=&quot;k-class2.png&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;K-Class Scenarios are hypothetical situations that could have drastic effects on normality or reality, including the &lt;em&gt;end of the world&lt;/em&gt;. The Foundation games out what can happen in these events, and authors on the wiki often reference these contingency plans&amp;#8230; or times they have failed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This collaborative page exists to document all K-Class Scenarios used on the wiki.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclaimers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;There is no canon definition for &lt;em&gt;any&lt;/em&gt; K-Class Scenario. This page should &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; be seen as a &amp;quot;canonical&amp;quot; resource. Please do not hassle authors for &amp;quot;misusing&amp;quot; these scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This list is meant to be &lt;em&gt;descriptive&lt;/em&gt;, not &lt;em&gt;prescriptive&lt;/em&gt;. Definitions are based on usage in articles, not what anyone &lt;em&gt;thinks&lt;/em&gt; they &lt;em&gt;should&lt;/em&gt; mean. (For earlier lists with invented definitions, scroll down.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A bit on notation:&lt;/strong&gt; (I treated any of these grammatical variants as equivalent.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;show&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;–&amp;nbsp;hide&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scenarios &lt;em&gt;generally&lt;/em&gt; follow: &amp;lt;Letter&amp;gt;K-Class &amp;lt;description/end-of-the-world&amp;gt; scenario&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;quot;K-class &lt;em&gt;scenario&lt;/em&gt;&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;K-class &lt;em&gt;event&lt;/em&gt;&amp;quot; seem to be used interchangeably. There&#039;s no consistent logic to it. Scenario was used about 4 times as often as event in my initial search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capitalization (XK-Class End&amp;#8230;, XK-class end&amp;#8230;) and truncation (end-of-the-world, &amp;quot;end of the world&amp;quot;, end of the world) don&#039;t seem to have any set standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;–&amp;nbsp;hide&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you want to help?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Please do! This is a collaboration. See the steps below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;So&amp;nbsp;you&amp;nbsp;want&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;link&amp;nbsp;an&amp;nbsp;article?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;–&amp;nbsp;hide&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So you want to link an article?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Please, please do this! My initial scraping only covered &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/k-class-scenario&quot;&gt;tagged&lt;/a&gt; SCPs, so tales and other articles need attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure the article is staying in the positive ratings (remaining at +1 or above for 24 hours) before adding the link: it&#039;s a pain to go through and clean up afterwards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the article uses an existing prefix and fits a common definition, just add the link and update the count (# SCPs, # Tales, # Others). Maybe add the Alternative title if it&#039;s new and sounds cool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the scenario is inconsistent with others in that prefix, OR is the first article using a prefix, OR only appears in a -J, please add it to the appropriate table using this format:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
&lt;code&gt;||~ Title ||~ Definition ||~ Articles ||
|| || || ||&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you need a whole tab, here is a basic format:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
&lt;code&gt;[[tab prefix]]
**Most Common:** 
**Used in:** # SCPs, # Tales, # Other
**Primary definition:** 
**Alternative titles:** 
**SCPs:** 
**Tales and other articles:**

**Inconsistent Uses**
||~ Title ||~ Definition ||~ Articles ||
||  || || ||
[[/tab]]&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;–&amp;nbsp;hide&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;So&amp;nbsp;you&amp;nbsp;want&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;add&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;update&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;definition?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;–&amp;nbsp;hide&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So you want to add or update a definition?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Maybe you were the author of a one-off or inconsistent-use scenario, or maybe you want to update a primary definition that is out of date. (Or, you know, if it could be better.) Go for it! Just remember:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Definitions should be &lt;em&gt;usage&lt;/em&gt;-based. Only create or update definitions to fit their use in articles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the usage and title is really different from its current prefix, consider adding it to &amp;quot;Inconsistent Uses&amp;quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It helps if you add a note down in the &amp;quot;Short description of changes:&amp;quot; before you hit &amp;quot;Save&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not add definitions without a successful, linked article!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;–&amp;nbsp;hide&amp;nbsp;block&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;div id=&quot;wiki-tabview-5278516a8f7d30dcbc39b12102a0f0ae&quot; class=&quot;yui-navset&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;yui-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;selected&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Scenarios With Multiple Uses&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;AK*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ADK&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;CK©&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EK*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;GK/GH©&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;HK*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;IK*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;LK*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;MK*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;NK©&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
