&lt;td style=&quot;border: 1px solid black; padding: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;03/26/2011 - 05/17/2011:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr. D. Sokolsky claims SCP-5109 for use as a research group FTP password. He instructs his colleagues to telephone him for a new, one-time password before uploading their data each day. He actually recites SCP-5109 to them each time, asking that they repeat it back to him before completing the log-on process. At the conclusion of the research project Dr. Sokolsky creates a new, non-anomalous password for the FTP system and returns SCP-5109 to Chief Veiksaar.&lt;/td&gt;
